### Create User 1
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Create User 2
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob",
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "bob123"
}

### Create User 3
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carlos",
  "email": "carlos@example.com",
  "password": "carlos123"
}

### Create User - email duplicado (deve dar 409)
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice2",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Create User - nome em branco (deve dar 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "  ",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Create User - email inválido (deve dar 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice",
  "email": "invalidemail.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Get User por id
GET http://localhost:8080/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{myToken}}

### Get User por id (Missing Token) (Should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/1

### Get User - id inexistente (deve dar 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/999
Authorization: Bearer {{myToken}}

### Get User - id inválido (deve dar 400)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{myToken}}

### Login (Success) (deve dar 200 com id e token)
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### Login - password errada (deve dar 401)
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Login - email inexistente (deve dar 404)
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "alice123"
}